nction\n   - Preserves all DSTAGNN components (attention, Chebyshev conv, GTU)\n   - Handles adjacency matrix from data_feature\n   - Properly handles device placement\n\n4. Update `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py` to register DSTAGNN\n\n**LibCity Batch Format** (critical for adaptation):\n- batch['X']: Input shape (batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n- batch['y']: Target shape (batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)\n- batch['X_ext']: External features (optional)\n- Note: You'll need to transpose from LibCity's (B, T, N, F) to DSTAGNN's (B, N, F, T)\n\n**Important Notes**:\n- DSTAGNN expects adjacency matrix - extract from `data_feature.get('adj_mx')`\n- Use self._scaler for normalization handling\n- Preserve the dynamic graph learning capability ('AG' mode)\n- Keep all attention mechanisms and multi-scale GTU intact\n- Use torch.nn.SmoothL1Loss as the original implementation does\n- Ensure all model components are properly moved to device\n\n**Reference LibCity Models**:\n- Check `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/GWNET.py` for graph convolution example\n- Check `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/ASTGCN.py` for attention mechanisms\n\nReport when complete with the file path created.", 'subagent_type': 'model-adapter'}
