[GraphMM:migration] 2026-02-04 10:04:24 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/documents/GraphMM_migration_summary.md', 'content': "# GraphMM Migration Summary\n\n## Overview\n\nGraphMM (Graph-based Map Matching) has been adapted from the original implementation to the LibCity framework. This model uses graph neural networks to encode both road network topology and trajectory point relationships for map matching tasks.\n\n## Original Source Files\n\n- **Main Model**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/model/gmm.py` (GMM class)\n- **Sub-modules**:\n  - RoadGIN: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/model/road_gin.py`\n  - TraceGCN: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/model/trace_gcn.py`\n  - Seq2Seq: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/model/seq2seq.py`\n  - CRF: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/model/crf.py`\n- **Data Loading**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/data_loader.py`\n- **Graph Data**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/graph_data.py`\n- **Config**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/GraphMM/config.py`\n\n## LibCity Target Files\n\n- **Model File**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/map_matching/GraphMM.py`\n- **Config File**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/map_matching/GraphMM.json`\n- **Init File**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/map_matching/__init__.py`\n\n## Key Changes Made\n\n### 1. Class Hierarchy\n\n- **Original**: `GMM` inherits from `nn.Module`\n- **Adapted**: `GraphMM` inherits from `AbstractModel` (LibCity base class)\n\n### 2. All Sub-modules Consolidated\n\nAll sub-modules (RoadGIN, GCNLayer, DiGCN, TraceGCN, Attention, Seq2Seq, CRF, GraphData) are now included in a single file to simplify imports and dependency management.\n\n### 3. Interface Methods\n\nAdded required LibCity methods:\n- `__init__(self, config, data_feature)`: Initializes model from config dict and data features\n- `predict(self, batch)`: Inference method for evaluation\n- `calculate_loss(self, batch)`: Computes training loss\n\n### 4. Data Format Adaptation\n\n**Original batch format** (from DataLoader):\n```python\n# data[0]: grid_traces (batch_size, seq_len)\n# data[1]: tgt_roads (batch_size, tgt_len)\n# data[2]: traces_gps (batch_size, seq_len, 2)\n# data[3]: sample_idx (batch_size, seq_len)\n# data[4]: trace_lens (list)\n# data[5]: road_lens (list)\n```\n\n**LibCity batch format** (dictionary):\n```python\nbatch = {\n    'grid_traces': tensor,     # Grid cell IDs\n    'tgt_roads': tensor,       # Target road sequence\n    'traces_gps': tensor,      # GPS coordinates\n    'sample_idx': tensor,      # Sampling indices\n    'trace_lens': list/tensor, # Actual trace lengths\n    'road_lens': list/tensor   # Actual road sequence lengths\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Graph Data Handling\n\n**Original**: `GraphData` class loaded from files in a specific directory structure\n**Adapted**: `GraphData` class initialized from `data_feature` dictionary\n\nRequired data_feature keys:\n- `num_roads`: Number of road segments\n- `num_grids`: Number of grid cells\n- `road_x`: Road features tensor (num_roads, feat_dim)\n- `road_adj`: Road adjacency SparseTensor\n- `trace_in_edge_index`, `trace_out_edge_index`: Trace graph edges\n- `trace_weight`: Trace graph edge weights\n- `map_matrix`: Grid to road mapping matrix\n- `singleton_grid_mask`: Mask for singleton grids\n- `singleton_grid_location`: GPS for singleton grids\n- `A_matrix`: Adjacency matrix for CRF\n\n### 6. Parameter Name Mapping\n\n| Original | LibCity |\n|----------|---------|\n| `drop_prob` | `dropout` |\n| `atten_flag` | `use_attention` |\n| `bi` | `bidirectional` |\n| `tf_ratio` | `teacher_forcing_ratio` |\n| `target_size` | `num_roads` (from data_feature) |\n\n## Model Architecture Summary\n\n```\nGraphMM\n  |-- RoadGIN (Road Network Encoder)\n  |     |-- Multiple GINConv layers with MLP\n  |     |-- BatchNorm + ReLU\n  |     |-- Max pooling across layers\n  |\n  |-- TraceGCN (Trajectory Grid Encoder)\n  |     |-- DiGCN for incoming edges\n  |     |-- DiGCN for outgoing edges\n  |     |-- Concatenate both directions\n  |\n  |-- Seq2Seq (Decoder)\n  |     |-- Bidirectional GRU Encoder\n  |     |-- Attention Mechanism\n  |     |-- GRU Decoder\n  |\n  |-- CRF (Optional Structured Prediction)\n        |-- Learnable transition matrix\n        |-- Negative sampling for training\n        |-- Viterbi decoding for inference\n```\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Default | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|\n| `emb_dim` | 256 | Embedding dimension |\n| `dropout` | 0.5 | Dropout probability |\n| `use_crf` | True | Whether to use CRF layer |\n| `use_attention` | True | Whether to use attention in seq2seq |\n| `bidirectional` | True | Whether to use bidirectional GRU |\n| `teacher_forcing_ratio` | 0.5 | Teacher forcing ratio for training |\n| `topn` | 5 | Top-n candidates for CRF decoding |\n| `neg_nums` | 800 | Negative sampling number |\n| `layer` | 4 | Hops for adjacency polynomial |\n| `gamma` | 10000 | Penalty for unreachable transitions |\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThe model requires:\n- PyTorch\n- torch_geometric (for GINConv, GCNConv, MLP)\n- torch_sparse (for SparseTensor)\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.map_matching import GraphMM\n\n# Configuration\nconfig = {\n    'device': 'cuda:0',\n    'emb_dim': 256,\n    'use_crf': True,\n    'dropout': 0.5,\n    # ... other parameters\n}\n\n# Data features (from dataset)\ndata_feature = {\n    'num_roads': 5000,\n    'num_grids': 10000,\n    'road_x': road_features_tensor,\n    'road_adj': road_adjacency_sparse,\n    # ... other graph data\n}\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = GraphMM(config, data_feature)\nmodel = model.to(config['device'])\n\n# Training\nfor batch in train_loader:\n    loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n    loss.backward()\n    optimizer.step()\n\n# Inference\nmodel.eval()\npredictions = model.predict(batch)\n```\n\n## Limitations and Notes\n\n1. **Graph Data Dependency**: The model requires pre-computed graph structures (road network, trace graph) to be provided in `data_feature`. A compatible dataset loader needs to prepare these structures.\n\n2. **CRF Negative Sampling**: The CRF layer uses negative sampling which assumes the number of sampled tags is less than `neg_nums`. This assertion may fail with very small batches.\n\n3. **Memory Usage**: The model maintains full road embeddings and adjacency matrices in memory, which may be memory-intensive for large road networks.\n\n4. **Teacher Forcing**: During training, teacher forcing ratio is applied randomly at each decoding step. For evaluation, teacher forcing is disabled (ratio=0).\n\n## Original Paper\n\nGraphMM: Graph-based Vehicular Map Matching by Leveraging Trajectory and Road Correlations\n\n## Metrics\n\nThe original implementation uses:\n- Point-wise accuracy: Percentage of correctly matched road segments\n- LCS (Longest Common Subsequence): Sequence-level matching quality\n"}
