[DiffMM:migration] 2026-02-04 10:28:31 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/documents/DiffMM_migration_summary.md', 'content': "# DiffMM Model Migration Summary\n\n## Overview\n\nDiffMM (Diffusion-based Map Matching) has been adapted from the original repository to LibCity framework for trajectory map matching tasks.\n\n## Source Repository\n\n- **Location:** `./repos/DiffMM/`\n- **Main Model Files:**\n  - `models/model.py` - TrajEncoder, ModelAllShortCut\n  - `models/short_cut.py` - ShortCut, DiT, DiTBlock\n  - `models/layers.py` - PointEncoder, Attention, Transformer components\n  - `models/diffusion.py` - GaussianDiffusion (not used in ShortCut version)\n\n## Target Location\n\n- **Model File:** `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/map_matching/DiffMM.py`\n- **Config File:** `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/map_matching/DiffMM.json`\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Components\n\n1. **TrajEncoder**\n   - Encodes GPS trajectory points with road segment embeddings\n   - Uses PointEncoder (Transformer-based) for GPS sequence encoding\n   - Computes attention over candidate road segments per GPS point\n   - Combines point embeddings with attended road segment embeddings\n   - Output: (batch, seq_len, 2*hid_dim)\n\n2. **DiT (Diffusion Transformer)**\n   - Transformer-based denoising network\n   - Uses AdaLN (Adaptive Layer Normalization) for conditioning\n   - Conditioned on trajectory embeddings and diffusion timesteps\n   - Multiple DiTBlock layers with self-attention and feed-forward\n\n3. **ShortCut**\n   - One-step diffusion model for efficient inference\n   - Uses flow matching with bootstrapping for training\n   - Combines MSE loss on velocity with BCE loss on predictions\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nGPS Points + Candidate Segments\n         |\n         v\n    TrajEncoder\n         |\n         v\nTrajectory Embeddings (condition)\n         |\n         v\n    DiT Denoiser\n         |\n         v\nRoad Segment Probabilities\n```\n\n## LibCity Integration\n\n### Base Class\n\n- Inherits from `AbstractModel`\n\n### Required Methods\n\n1. `__init__(config, data_feature)` - Initialize model\n2. `forward(batch)` - Training forward pass, returns loss\n3. `predict(batch)` - Inference, returns predictions\n4. `calculate_loss(batch)` - Returns training loss (calls forward)\n\n### Batch Format\n\nThe model expects a batch dictionary with:\n\n```python\nbatch = {\n    'src': torch.Tensor,        # GPS points (batch, seq_len, 3)\n    'src_len': list or Tensor,  # Sequence lengths\n    'src_segs': torch.Tensor,   # Candidate segment IDs (batch, seq_len, num_cands)\n    'segs_feat': torch.Tensor,  # Segment features (batch, seq_len, num_cands, 9)\n    'segs_mask': torch.Tensor,  # Valid segment mask (batch, seq_len, num_cands)\n    'target': torch.Tensor,     # Target one-hot (batch, seq_len, num_cands)\n}\n```\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| hid_dim | int | 256 | Hidden dimension |\n| num_units | int | 512 | Number of units for denoiser |\n| transformer_layers | int | 2 | Number of transformer layers in PointEncoder |\n| depth | int | 2 | Number of DiT blocks |\n| timesteps | int | 2 | Diffusion timesteps for training |\n| samplingsteps | int | 1 | Inference steps for diffusion |\n| dropout | float | 0.1 | Dropout probability |\n| bootstrap_every | int | 8 | Bootstrap frequency for training |\n| num_heads | int | 4 | Number of attention heads |\n| num_cands | int | 10 | Number of candidate segments per point |\n\n## Required Data Features\n\n| Feature | Type | Description |\n|---------|------|-------------|\n| id_size | int | Number of unique road segment IDs |\n| num_cands | int | Maximum number of candidate segments (if not in config) |\n\n## Key Changes from Original\n\n1. **Class Structure:**\n   - Combined ModelAllShortCut with DiffMM as single class\n   - Moved all layer classes into single file\n\n2. **Device Handling:**\n   - Uses `config.get('device')` instead of hardcoded device\n\n3. **Batch Interface:**\n   - Adapted from custom data loader to LibCity batch dictionary\n\n4. **Loss Computation:**\n   - Integrated loss calculation into `forward()` and `calculate_loss()`\n\n5. **Inference:**\n   - Added `predict()` method for LibCity evaluation\n   - Returns argmax predictions for evaluation metrics\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.map_matching import DiffMM\n\nconfig = {\n    'device': 'cuda',\n    'hid_dim': 256,\n    'depth': 2,\n    'timesteps': 2,\n    'samplingsteps': 1,\n    'num_cands': 10\n}\n\ndata_feature = {\n    'id_size': 10000,\n    'num_cands': 10\n}\n\nmodel = DiffMM(config, data_feature)\nmodel = model.to(config['device'])\n\n# Training\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\nloss.backward()\n\n# Inference\npredictions = model.predict(batch)\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- PyTorch (torch, torch.nn, torch.nn.functional)\n- Standard Python libraries (math, logging)\n\n## Notes\n\n- The model uses a one-step diffusion approach (ShortCut) for efficiency\n- Bootstrapping is used during training for distillation\n- The 9D road segment features include geometric and topological attributes\n- GPS points have 3 features: latitude, longitude, and optionally timestamp\n"}
