[GraphMM:migration] 2026-02-04 10:28:42 | INFO | Tool Task called with {'prompt': "Fix the adjacency matrix key mismatch in GraphMM's GraphData class.\n\n## Problem\nThe dataset provides `A_list` (pre-computed adjacency polynomial) but GraphData expects `A_matrix` (raw adjacency matrix), causing A_list to be None and leading to a TypeError during forward pass.\n\n## Fix Required\nFile: Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/map_matching/GraphMM.py\n\nLocation: Lines 625-630 in `GraphData.__init__()` method\n\n**Current code (around line 625-630):**\n```python\n# Adjacency polynomial\nA = data_feature.get('A_matrix')\nself.A_list = self._get_adj_poly(A, layer, gamma) if A is not None else None\n```\n\n**Replace with:**\n```python\n# Adjacency polynomial\nA = data_feature.get('A_matrix')\nif A is not None:\n    self.A_list = self._get_adj_poly(A, layer, gamma)\nelse:\n    # Fall back to pre-computed A_list from dataset\n    self.A_list = data_feature.get('A_list')\n    if self.A_list is not None:\n        self.A_list = self.A_list.to(device)\n```\n\n## Rationale\nThis allows GraphData to accept either:\n1. Raw adjacency matrix (`A_matrix`) and compute the polynomial itself, OR\n2. Pre-computed adjacency polynomial (`A_list`) directly from the dataset\n\nThis makes the model compatible with LibCity's DeepMapMatchingDataset which provides the pre-computed version.\n\nPlease apply this fix.", 'subagent_type': 'model-adapter', 'description': 'Fix GraphData A_list issue'}
[GraphMM:migration] 2026-02-04 10:28:42 | INFO | Assistant: Fix the adjacency matrix key mismatch in GraphMM's GraphData class.
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] ## Problem
[GraphMM:migration] The dataset provides `A_list` (pre-computed adjacency polynomial) but GraphData expects `A_matrix` (raw adjacency matrix), causing A_list to be None and leading to a TypeError during forward pass.
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] ## Fix Required
[GraphMM:migration] File: Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/map_matching/GraphMM.py
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] Location: Lines 625-630 in `GraphData.__init__()` method
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] **Current code (around line 625-630):**
[GraphMM:migration] ```python
[GraphMM:migration] # Adjacency polynomial
[GraphMM:migration] A = data_feature.get('A_matrix')
[GraphMM:migration] self.A_list = self._get_adj_poly(A, layer, gamma) if A is not None else None
[GraphMM:migration] ```
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] **Replace with:**
[GraphMM:migration] ```python
[GraphMM:migration] # Adjacency polynomial
[GraphMM:migration] A = data_feature.get('A_matrix')
[GraphMM:migration] if A is not None:
[GraphMM:migration]     self.A_list = self._get_adj_poly(A, layer, gamma)
[GraphMM:migration] else:
[GraphMM:migration]     # Fall back to pre-computed A_list from dataset
[GraphMM:migration]     self.A_list = data_feature.get('A_list')
[GraphMM:migration]     if self.A_list is not None:
[GraphMM:migration]         self.A_list = self.A_list.to(device)
[GraphMM:migration] ```
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] ## Rationale
[GraphMM:migration] This allows GraphData to accept either:
[GraphMM:migration] 1. Raw adjacency matrix (`A_matrix`) and compute the polynomial itself, OR
[GraphMM:migration] 2. Pre-computed adjacency polynomial (`A_list`) directly from the dataset
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] This makes the model compatible with LibCity's DeepMapMatchingDataset which provides the pre-computed version.
[GraphMM:migration] 
[GraphMM:migration] Please apply this fix.
