[DeepMM:migration] 2026-02-04 10:35:56 | INFO | Tool Task called with {'description': 'Fix DeepMM predict method output', 'prompt': 'Fix the DeepMM model\'s predict() method to return predicted indices instead of logits.\n\n**Issue:**\nThe `predict()` method returns 3D logits `[batch, seq_len, vocab_size=183]` but the executor expects 2D predicted indices `[batch, seq_len]`.\n\n**Fix Required:**\n\nFile: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/trajectory_loc_prediction/DeepMM.py`\n\nLocate the `predict()` method (around lines 543-548) and modify it:\n\n**Current code:**\n```python\ndef predict(self, batch):\n    """Generate predictions for a batch."""\n    if \'input_trg\' in batch:\n        logits = self.forward(batch)\n        return logits  # Returns 3D: [batch, seq_len, vocab_size]\n    else:\n        return self.greedy_decode(batch)\n```\n\n**Change to:**\n```python\ndef predict(self, batch):\n    """Generate predictions for a batch."""\n    if \'input_trg\' in batch:\n        logits = self.forward(batch)\n        # Return predicted indices, not logits\n        return logits.argmax(dim=-1)  # Returns 2D: [batch, seq_len]\n    else:\n        return self.greedy_decode(batch)\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- `logits.argmax(dim=-1)` converts the 3D logits tensor to 2D by taking the most likely road segment ID at each position\n- This matches what the executor expects for accuracy calculation\n- The greedy_decode path already returns indices, so it doesn\'t need changes\n\nThis is a simple one-line fix that will allow evaluation to proceed correctly.', 'subagent_type': 'model-adapter'}
